+# Block catalog: CanvasGroup count
+
+## Problem
+
+On phones at low graphics quality, the catalog flickered and some cards drew blank. With it
+open, PlayerGui held 41 CanvasGroups: the panel plus one per card (5 block types x 8 shapes).
+All CanvasGroups share one texture budget, and the client's quality level caps it. Past the
+budget, groups blur, flicker, or draw blank. PC runs at a higher quality level, so it had
+room for all 41.
+
+## Change
+
+`src/StarterPlayer/StarterPlayerScripts/BlockCatalog.luau`
+
+- Each card is now a plain `Frame` with a `UICorner`. Its swatch, labels, and hitbox are
+  unchanged.
+- The shine stripe sits in its own `ShineClip` CanvasGroup, with the card's corner radius, built
+  with `show` only while that card's shine is above 0: while it is hovered, and while the shine
+  fades out after the cursor leaves. That group still clips the rotated stripe to the rounded
+  corners. A plain `ClipsDescendants` frame would clip to the rectangle and ignore both the
+  `UICorner` and the rotation.
+- The shine fade now drives the group's `GroupTransparency` (`1 - shine`) instead of the
+  stripe's own transparency, and the stripe stays at 0.5. Strength works out the same as
+  before (half opacity at full shine). Because the group is almost fully clear when it is
+  created and when it is removed, the white frame a CanvasGroup can draw at those moments
+  doesn't show.
+- The panel keeps its CanvasGroup for the fade in and out. It already existed only while the
+  catalog was open (`show` in `Main.client.luau`). Fading each element on its own would look
+  different wherever the cards overlap the panel background.
+
+Expected count: 1 CanvasGroup with the catalog open and idle, 2 while a card is hovered (a few
+more briefly while shines fade out after quick sweeps over several cards), and 0 with the
+catalog closed. Before the change it was 41 whenever the catalog was open.
+
+## How to check
+
+1. Play in Studio, open the catalog (C or the Catalog button), and run this in the command bar
+   (client side):
+
+   ```lua
+   local total, drawn = 0, 0
+   for _, instance in game.Players.LocalPlayer.PlayerGui:GetDescendants() do
+   	if instance:IsA("CanvasGroup") then
+   		total += 1
+   		print(instance:GetFullName())
+   	end
+   end
+   print("CanvasGroups:", total)
+   ```
+
+   Expect 1 (`BlockCatalog`). Hover a card and run it again: expect 2 (`...ShineClip`). Close the
+   catalog and wait for the fade: expect 0.
+2. Look: the panel still fades in and out. On hover, the shine sweeps across the card, clipped
+   to its rounded corners at all four corners. When the cursor leaves, the shine slides back
+   and fades. Watch the first and last frames of a hover for any white flash.
+3. On a phone, or in Studio's device emulator with Settings > Graphics Quality set to 1: open
+   the catalog, scroll through every card, and confirm none flicker or draw blank.
